Falsifies `periodic_deadline::proofs::a_fire_is_strictly_in_the_future`.

The defect: the first-candidate test accepts a candidate that merely reaches `now`, `first >= now`
in place of `first > now`. Both spellings read as "the first occurrence has not happened yet", and
they differ only when `prev + period` lands exactly on `now`, which is the case a polling
scheduler hits every time it wakes on the beat instead of late.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(next > now)`, at `prev + period == now`, where the
function returns `now` itself and the same occurrence fires again on the next poll.

